Subject: [PATCH] ARM: extend the module address space

Large proprietary receiver drivers and the networking and filesystem modules
exhaust the 14 MiB module area. Loading rtl8852cu needs another 6.1 MiB and
fails in module_alloc() despite sufficient physical memory.

Reserve 24 MiB below PAGE_OFFSET instead of 16 MiB. With CONFIG_HIGHMEM, the
existing 2 MiB pkmap reservation leaves 22 MiB for modules.

Lower TASK_SIZE to PAGE_OFFSET - SZ_32M, not MODULES_VADDR: svc_entry in
entry-armv.S loads it with a single ARM MOV immediate. With a PAGE_OFFSET of
0xc0000000, 0xbe800000 is not encodable, while 0xbe000000 is. The 8 MiB
virtual gap below MODULES_VADDR does not reserve physical RAM.

A module at MODULES_VADDR has to reach the end of the kernel text with a
32 MiB branch, so the kernel text must stay below 8 MiB. Module PLTs stay
disabled, so the vendor module ABI does not change.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [machine-specific address-space layout]

--- a/arch/arm/include/asm/memory.h
+++ b/arch/arm/include/asm/memory.h
@@ -36,8 +36,10 @@
 /*
  * TASK_SIZE - the maximum size of a user space task.
  * TASK_UNMAPPED_BASE - the lower boundary of the mmap VM area
+ * Keep TASK_SIZE encodable as an ARM MOV immediate in entry-armv.S.
+ * The gap below MODULES_VADDR does not reserve physical RAM.
  */
-#define TASK_SIZE		(UL(CONFIG_PAGE_OFFSET) - UL(SZ_16M))
+#define TASK_SIZE		(UL(CONFIG_PAGE_OFFSET) - UL(SZ_32M))
 #define TASK_UNMAPPED_BASE	ALIGN(TASK_SIZE / 3, SZ_16M)
 
 /*
@@ -50,7 +52,7 @@
  * and PAGE_OFFSET - it must be within 32MB of the kernel text.
  */
 #ifndef CONFIG_THUMB2_KERNEL
-#define MODULES_VADDR		(PAGE_OFFSET - SZ_16M)
+#define MODULES_VADDR		(PAGE_OFFSET - SZ_16M - SZ_8M)
 #else
 /* smaller range for Thumb-2 symbols relocation (2^24)*/
 #define MODULES_VADDR		(PAGE_OFFSET - SZ_8M)
